

CapCut’s effect library is large, dynamic, and version-dependent, so there usually isn’t one fixed public master list that stays accurate across mobile vs desktop, free vs Pro, and region-specific builds.

I checked current CapCut sources and confirmed two useful things:

CapCut is actively promoting AI effects and frequently rotating new/trending effects
CapCut’s official current help content also highlights trending transition families like velocity, beat sync, glitch/digital distortion, and cinematic fade/zoom — which are related, but not the same as video effects

So the most honest and useful answer is this: below is a comprehensive practical list of CapCut video effect types and common effect families you can expect to find, rather than a claim that every single preset name is identical in every installation.

